    <h1>NYC Taxi Lakehouse</h1>
    <p class="taxi-deck">Public trip files. Accountable data. Inspectable results.</p>
    <p>A Databricks lakehouse built around source-month processing: ingest public yellow-taxi files, separate rejected records, model accepted trips, and reconcile the result before reporting.</p>
    <div class="taxi-status"><strong id="taxi-publication-label">Source-month coverage</strong><span id="taxi-verification-date">32 source months</span><span id="taxi-coverage">January 2024 &ndash; August 2026</span></div>
    <p class="taxi-muted" id="taxi-publication-note">Verified snapshot of monthly source data, not a live public feed. Scheduled availability checks process eligible new or changed monthly files.</p>
    <nav class="taxi-local-nav" aria-label="Project sections"><a href="#architecture">Pipeline</a><a href="#results">Results</a><a href="#quality">Quality</a><a href="#operations">Operations</a><a href="#source">Inspect the work</a></nav>
  </header>
  <section class="taxi-band" id="architecture">
    <p class="taxi-kicker">01 / Architecture</p><h2>From source to dashboard</h2>
    <ol class="taxi-flow">
      <li><a href="#stage-source"><small>01 / Source</small><strong>TLC Parquet</strong><span>Monthly yellow-taxi files</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="#stage-bronze"><small>02 / Ingestion</small><strong>Landing + Bronze</strong><span>Preserve provenance</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="#stage-silver"><small>03 / Quality</small><strong>Silver + quarantine</strong><span>Accept or isolate</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="#stage-gold"><small>04 / Modeling</small><strong>Gold + checks</strong><span>Reconcile rows and cents</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="#stage-dashboard"><small>05 / Consumption</small><strong>Dashboard</strong><span>Analytics and operations</span></a></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="taxi-stage-list">
      <details id="stage-source" open><summary>Source and publication eligibility</summary><p>Official NYC TLC yellow-taxi trip records arrive as monthly Parquet files. The runner computes the latest due source period, then checks publication availability. A missing file is a waiting state, not proof of an empty month.</p><p><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/site/tlc/about/tlc-trip-record-data.page">Official TLC trip-record source &nearr;</a> &middot; <a href="/assets/project-code/08_monthly_pipeline_runner.py" download>Runner notebook</a></p></details>
      <details id="stage-bronze"><summary>Landing and Bronze: traceable ingestion</summary><p>Files are landed before ingestion. Bronze retains source and batch metadata so each monthly input can be traced through later stages. Processing is bounded by source period rather than pickup date alone.</p><p><a href="/assets/project-code/02_ingest_to_bronze.py" download>Ingestion notebook</a></p></details>
      <details id="stage-silver"><summary>Silver and quarantine: explicit quality policy</summary><p>Quality rules separate accepted trips from rejected evidence. Negative amounts are among the exclusions; this changes the population represented by accepted totals. Boundary-date observations are tracked separately from dates outside the allowed grace window.</p><p><a href="/assets/project-code/03_quality_checks.py" download>Quality checks</a> &middot; <a href="/assets/project-code/04_transform_to_silver.py" download>Silver transformation</a></p></details>
      <details id="stage-gold"><summary>Gold and reconciliation: prove the handoff</summary><p>Gold models accepted trips for reporting. Reconciliation checks the Bronze split, Silver-to-Gold row preservation, amounts in cents, date windows, and required metadata. Source-month accounting preserves historical coverage.</p><p><a href="/assets/project-code/05_build_gold_model.py" download>Gold model</a> &middot; <a href="/assets/project-code/06_reconciliation_and_audit.py" download>Reconciliation notebook</a></p></details>
      <details id="stage-dashboard"><summary>Analytics and pipeline operations</summary><p>The native Databricks dashboard separates Lakehouse analytics from Operations. Filters use source periods. Event counts describe an observed stage and are not automatically current table counts.</p><p><a href="/assets/project-code/07_reporting_queries.py" download>Reporting queries</a> &middot; <a href="/assets/project-code/10_backfill_status.py" download>Backfill status notebook</a></p></details>
    </div>
  </section>
