  <section class="taxi-band" id="quality">
    <p class="taxi-kicker">03 / Data quality</p><h2>Account for every source row</h2>
    <p class="taxi-muted" id="taxi-quality-range">Source-month accounting: January 2024 through August 2026.</p>
    <dl class="taxi-proof"><div><dt>Bronze = Silver + quarantine</dt><dd id="taxi-quality-equation">119,595,677 = 115,842,411 + 3,753,266</dd></div><div><dt>Silver = Gold</dt><dd id="taxi-quality-preservation">115,842,411 rows in each</dd></div><div><dt>Boundary observations</dt><dd id="taxi-quality-boundary">661 accepted pickup-date observations outside their nominal source month</dd></div><div><dt>Weighted quarantine percentage</dt><dd id="taxi-quality-rate">3.14% = total quarantine / total Bronze</dd></div></dl>
    <p class="taxi-muted">Boundary observations are retained according to the date policy; they are not globally unique trips. These figures describe row accounting, not the status of every individual quality rule.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="taxi-band" id="operations">
    <p class="taxi-kicker">04 / Orchestration</p><h2>Scheduled checks, bounded work</h2>
    <dl class="taxi-proof"><div><dt>Source availability check</dt><dd>Daily at 09:00 Asia/Calcutta (UTC+05:30)</dd></div><div><dt>When new or changed files are found</dt><dd>Process eligible source months, reconcile the results, then publish the updated monthly report.</dd></div><div><dt>When files have not changed</dt><dd>Skip ETL and keep the existing report; a daily check does not mean new data was processed.</dd></div><div><dt>Task order</dt><dd>Monthly runner, followed by the summary publisher on upstream success.</dd></div><div><dt>Concurrent runs</dt><dd>1, with queue enabled</dd></div></dl>
  </section>
